*** CORRECTED 2026-09-16 FROM CLOSING PASS 5 -- THIS FLOOR LINE IS THE RECORD A FUTURE READER WILL TRUST, AND IT
         INHERITS FOUR WRONG CLAIMS FROM THE PROBE HEADER.  Measured in artifacts/lcaisalane/opus_c5_20260915/
         OPUS_ANSWER.md; the header itself is corrected in place. ***
         1. "the forward-count class CLOSED BY ENUMERATION" -- the class is EIGHT cells ({write, read} x {DROP, SWAP,
            DUPLICATE, ADD-OTHER}, derived from the single bus forward each arm emits); the contract enumerates TWO.
            The write arm's DUPLICATE escapes at the tails and at len 6 (WWtail, WW6, both 185/185).
         2. "every one rowed" -- false for the write-DUPLICATE and read-ADD cells: at lanes 0/1/2 they are rowed by
            the emulator-TODO stub ALONE, which the same header forbids.
         3. the contract's "never as the sole carrier" (two sites) -- MEASURED FALSE THREE TIMES: WWall 169/185 is
            sixteen stub rows and NOTHING else; RWall 167/185 is 16 stub + 2 tailr; RD2post 161/185 has no
            architectural carrier at lanes 1-2.  CAUSE: CMOS REG C and ns16550 IIR are ONE-SHOT LATCHES, and a latch
            separates ZERO accesses from AT LEAST ONE -- it can never separate ONE from TWO, which is the whole
            question a forward-COUNT class asks.
         4. "the data axis's zero/nonzero partition rowed on both sides" -- a MARGINAL, not the per-cell claim it
            reads as.  Three joints measured empty: cdxZL3, dNZtail, RD2z, all 185/185.
         NOT CHANGED BY ANY OF THIS: HEAD_r6 112/185 and FIX_r6 185/185 are correct and were re-verified, and the FIX
         itself is correct and untouched -- six passes agree.  Every finding is against the DETECTOR and its record.
NOT RE-MEASURED  every table 1-5 kill: repair 5 ADDS sessions and changes no existing session's commands (the targeting
